<figure id="whole-train-clearance" class="article-figure">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 960 420"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="clearance-title clearance-desc"
    xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
  >
    <title id="clearance-title">A long train partly clearing a junction</title>
    <desc id="clearance-desc">
      A leading train extends from the approach through a junction onto the outgoing track. Its front has passed the
      junction, but its rear remains on the approach. A second train approaches on a conflicting path.
    </desc>

    <g class="figure-grid" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M80 70H880M80 140H880M80 210H880M80 280H880M80 350H880" />
      <path d="M160 45V375M320 45V375M480 45V375M640 45V375M800 45V375" />
    </g>

    <g class="figure-track" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M70 180H890" />
      <path d="M70 300H300C405 300 420 180 510 180" />
    </g>

    <g class="figure-junction" aria-hidden="true">
      <circle cx="510" cy="180" r="9" />
      <path d="M510 153V207M483 180H537" />
    </g>

    <g class="figure-train figure-train-leading" aria-hidden="true">
      <rect x="365" y="157" width="270" height="46" rx="3" />
      <path d="M635 157L667 180L635 203Z" />
      <path d="M394 168V192M424 168V192M454 168V192M484 168V192M514 168V192M544 168V192M574 168V192M604 168V192" />
    </g>

    <g class="figure-train figure-train-approaching" aria-hidden="true">
      <rect x="170" y="277" width="155" height="46" rx="3" />
      <path d="M325 277L357 300L325 323Z" />
      <path d="M198 288V312M228 288V312M258 288V312M288 288V312" />
    </g>

    <g class="figure-labels" aria-hidden="true">
      <text x="365" y="134">Leading train</text>
      <text x="170" y="355">Approaching train</text>
      <text x="526" y="236">Junction</text>
      <path d="M510 217V228" />
      <text x="633" y="132">Front</text>
      <path d="M650 139L650 153" />
      <text x="344" y="132">Rear</text>
      <path d="M375 139L375 153" />
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>Crossing a boundary is not the same as clearing it.</strong> A leading train has crossed a junction with
    its front while its rear remains on the approach. A second train is approaching on a conflicting path.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
